# Fuller Learning Companion — environment variables
#
# Every variable here is optional. The prototype runs with no .env file at all.
# Copy to .env.local to override.
#
# No API keys or secrets are read anywhere in this codebase. If you add a real AI
# provider, read its credentials from the environment and never commit them.


# Where the prototype SQLite database lives.
# A relative path resolves under the working directory; absolute paths are used
# as given. Deleting this file and restarting re-seeds the demonstration data,
# or run `npm run db:reset`.
#
# PROTOTYPE_DB_PATH=.data/prototype.db


# Base URL used when generating student join links and QR codes.
#
# Set this whenever you demo from a machine other than the one scanning the code.
# Left unset, QR codes point at http://localhost:3000, which a phone cannot reach.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000


# Which AI provider to use.
#
# `prototype` (the default) calls no model. It restructures content the professor
# already entered and labels every result as sample output.
#
# Any unrecognised value logs a warning and falls back to `prototype`. It will not
# throw at request time, and it will not pretend a model is running — /about shows
# the requested value alongside a note that it is not implemented.
#
# See docs/ai-integration-plan.md before adding a real provider: sending course
# material or student activity to a third party is a disclosure of education
# records and needs a data-processing agreement first.
#
# AI_PROVIDER=prototype


# Shared access password for a hosted demo.
#
# When set, the ENTIRE site sits behind one password: any request without a valid
# cookie is redirected to /unlock. Unset (the default) disables the gate completely,
# so local development and the test suites are unaffected.
#
# This is NOT authentication. It is one password shared by everyone with the link,
# with no identity, no roles and no audit trail. Its only job is to stop a public URL
# being stumbled upon or forwarded onward, because the professor portal has no login
# and shows student-shaped records. Real authentication is described in
# docs/future-authentication-plan.md and remains a prerequisite for real student data.
#
# DEMO_ACCESS_PASSWORD=choose-something-memorable


# Public base URL, read at RUNTIME.
#
# Prefer this over NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL for anything deployed: NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are
# inlined by Next during the build, so they cannot reflect a hostname that only exists
# once the service is created. Student join links and QR codes depend on getting this
# right.
#
# On Render you do not need to set it at all -- the app falls back to Render's own
# RENDER_EXTERNAL_URL.
#
# APP_URL=https://fuller-learning-companion.onrender.com
